---
layout: base.njk
title: Decoder
description: Partner-speak, translated — what AWS alliance vocabulary means in plain English, and what it actually means in the room.
---
<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap band__grid">
    <div class="rail">
      <p class="mono-label">Partner-speak,<br />translated</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>The Decoder</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Every alliance runs on vocabulary that means one thing in the documentation and
        something more specific in the room. Here's both, for the terms that come up most.
      </p>
      <p>
        I say all of these too. That's rather the point &mdash; the words aren't the problem,
        it's that nobody tells you what they're actually doing until you've sat through
        enough meetings to work it out.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--ruled band--tint">
  <div class="wrap band__grid">
    <div class="rail">
      <p class="mono-label">Hover or tap<br />any term</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="decoder">
        {% for item in decoder %}
        <button class="dterm" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
          <span class="dterm__grid">
            <span class="mono-label dterm__term">{{ item.term }}</span>
            <span class="dterm__body">
              <span class="dterm__plain">{{ item.plain }}</span>
              <span class="dterm__real">
                <span class="mono-label dterm__reallabel">What it actually means</span>
                {{ item.real }}
              </span>
            </span>
          </span>
        </button>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>

      <p class="decoder__foot mono-label">
        Missing one? <a href="/contact/">Send it to me</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
